# Ansible Development Guidelines

## Playbook Structure
- All tasks must use FQCN (Fully Qualified Collection Names)
- Use lowercase true/false for boolean values
- All playbooks should start with a clear description comment block
- Use meaningful play names that describe the purpose
- Organize tasks in logical blocks with clear names
- Include proper error handling with rescue and always blocks
- Use no_log: true for sensitive operations (tokens, credentials)

## Variable Management
- Define required variables at the start of the playbook
- Use assert tasks to validate required variables
- Document optional variables with default values
- Use proper variable scoping (host_vars, group_vars, playbook vars)

## Role Usage
- Include roles using ansible.builtin.include_role
- Specify tasks_from when including specific task files
- Maintain separation of concerns between roles
- Use common role for shared functionality

## Security Best Practices
- Never log sensitive information (tokens, credentials)
- Use validate_certs for HTTPS operations
- Implement proper error handling and validation
- Use secure variable handling for sensitive data

## Task Organization
- Group related tasks in blocks
- Use meaningful task names
- Include proper error handling
- Register results for important operations
- Use proper task delegation when needed

## Documentation
- Include clear descriptions for plays and tasks
- Document required and optional variables
- Add comments for complex operations
- Include examples in comments where helpful

## Error Handling
- Use block/rescue/always for error handling
- Provide clear error messages
- Log appropriate debug information
- Set operation status flags for tracking

## Code Style
- Use consistent indentation (2 spaces)
- Follow YAML best practices
- Use clear and consistent naming conventions
- Maintain proper spacing and organization

## Testing
- Include proper validation steps
- Use assert tasks for input validation
- Implement proper error checking
- Include debug tasks for troubleshooting

## Best Practices
- Use idempotent operations where possible
- Implement proper state checking
- Use proper task delegation
- Follow the principle of least privilege
- Implement proper logging and monitoring